Both registers and shared memory prevent a third CTA.  Three resident CTAs
would require at most 80 allocated registers/thread and about 32 KiB of
application shared memory per CTA after accounting for driver overhead.

Notes
-----

- The 87.92% elapsed-cycle value is the primary whole-kernel HMMA pipeline
  utilization.  The 88.55% active-cycle value excludes periods when the SM is
  inactive.
- Long-scoreboard stalls occupy 2.63% of active-warp cycles, so this profile
  does not indicate a dominant long-latency memory-dependency bottleneck.
- The test program's profiler-injected wall time is not meaningful because NCU
  replays and serializes the launch.  Use gpu__time_duration.sum (13.35 ms).
- Resource profiling used a one-CTA grid because launch resources do not depend
  on problem size.  Its measured achieved occupancy is intentionally ignored;
  the 33.33% theoretical occupancy applies to the full benchmark grid.
- The source default was subsequently changed from GROUP_M=4 to GROUP_M=6.
  Register/shared-memory resources are unchanged, but the L2, DRAM, stall, and
  HMMA counters above remain the GROUP_M=4 measurement snapshot.

